  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Reason for Refusal\r\n\r\nIt is considered that the proposed roof dormer extension, by way of its position, design and appearance, will have a detrimental effect on the appearance of both the dwellinghouse and the surrounding locality, as the site has a dual frontage, which makes it highly visible from public view.   It therefore does not have due regard for the sites unique characteristics and will be detrimental to the amenity of both the adjoining properties and the locality, contrary to Adopted UDP policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development) H.4.1 (Housing standards and Guidelines) and H.6.4 (Extensions and Alterations) of The London Borough of Hounslow UDP, Adopted December 2003 and supplementary planning guidelines."
